<title>POLAND: Jelfa plunges 9.6 pct on issue price news.</title>
<headline>Jelfa plunges 9.6 pct on issue price news.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish pharmaceuticals firm Jelfa SA shed 9.6 percent to 71 zlotys in moderate trade after the company on Friday priced its new share issue at 65 zlotys each, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue price caused today's fall, but we can't rule out that it will rebound soon as currently it's very difficult to buy anything on the primary market as many new issues have been heavily oversubscribed,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
